### Manual API walkthrough — works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension
### (or JetBrains' built-in HTTP client). Start the server first: npm run dev
###
### Prereqs: DB migrated + seeded (npm run prisma:seed) -> admin / ChangeMe123!
### For the /employees calls, put a REAL branch UUID from your DB in @branchId.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1
@branchId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### 0. Health
GET http://localhost:4000/health

### 1. Login as the seeded ADMIN
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "ChangeMe123!" }

###
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
@adminRefresh = {{adminLogin.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 2. Who am I?
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3. Sign up a gamer (public)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "demo_gamer", "password": "Password123!" }

### 4. Login as that gamer
# @name gamerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "demo_gamer", "password": "Password123!" }

###
@gamerToken = {{gamerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
@gamerId = {{gamerLogin.response.body.user.id}}

### 5. Gamer reads own profile -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{gamerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{gamerToken}}

### 6. Gamer tries to create an employee -> 403 FORBIDDEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{gamerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "branchId": "{{branchId}}", "username": "demo_emp", "password": "Password123!", "role": "EMPLOYEE" }

### 7. Admin creates a MANAGER -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "branchId": "{{branchId}}", "username": "demo_manager", "password": "Password123!", "role": "MANAGER" }

### 8. Admin promotes the gamer -> 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{gamerId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "EMPLOYEE" }

### 9. Refresh (rotates the token; run it twice to see REFRESH_TOKEN_REVOKED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{adminRefresh}}" }

### 10. Logout (revokes the refresh token) -> 204
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{adminRefresh}}" }
